        "message": "Navigating a shared friend circle right after a breakup is tricky, but you don't have to figure out long-term group dynamics today. Here is how to handle the immediate social side: 1. **Mute shared group chats:** Give yourself space from the stream of notifications without having to make a dramatic exit or explain yourself. You can check back in when you choose to.\n2. **Talk to one or two people privately:** If there are specific friends in the circle you trust completely, let them know one-on-one. You don't have to broadcast the news to everyone at once, and it helps to have an individual outlet.\n3. **Keep initial updates brief and neutral:** If people ask, a simple, non-detailed statement works best right now (for example: *\"We broke up yesterday. I'm taking some quiet time to process, so I might be offline for a bit.\"*). This prevents friends from feeling forced into picking sides before you even have your bearings. Are there upcoming group events or plans on the calendar, or is this mostly about daily group chats?",
